# family_house
:the_family
* Take a house for the family as well, with room for all of them and a hall [once] ?if coven_path() and can_acquire("coven_house")
  $ do acquire("coven_house")
  $ standing += 1
  It is a thing that a family needs, and has rarely been given. It has a long table, and a door that locks from the inside, and a hall that smells of coal smoke and beeswax. You notice that it has been furnished, in advance, by someone who has a very good eye for what people like.
* Put a front over the stables, a livery and a farrier with a sign [once] ?if can_acquire("front_business")
  $ do acquire("front_business")
  $ secrecy += 1
  It is a perfectly honest business. It has seven horses and a very good farrier, and in the loft above the hay there is a room that is entered by no stair.
* That is enough for now
  <~
-> :the_family

# tasks
?if coven_size() > 0
  The family are all of them eager, in the odd, unspoken way of a people who have spent twenty years on a patient errand and are at last allowed to do something with their hands.
  ?if in_circle("prisca") and member("prisca", "status") == "active"
    Prisca wants the books of the East End: who owes what to whom, and which landlords are paid and which are not. She says that a city can be read like a ledger, from the bottom.
    $ do coven_task("prisca", "watch")
  ?end
  ?if in_circle("fiammetta") and member("fiammetta", "status") == "active"
    Fiammetta wants the door. She says that she will not be surprised by a London again, and she has already walked the lane twice with a measuring stick.
    $ do coven_task("fiammetta", "guard")
  ?end
  ?if in_circle("hanno") and member("hanno", "status") == "active"
    Hanno wants the firm. He has said so with a nod. He has been looking at the ledgers of Collins and Hale in the way that an old dog looks at a new hearth.
    $ do coven_task("hanno", "business")
  ?end
  They are your arm in a city where you do not yet have a hand. It is the oldest of your instincts and the most necessary. You tell them that nobody is to act alone. They agree, in the voices of people who have been agreeing to that for a very long time.
?end
