# dawn
## Before the dark ends
$ do discover("the_jubilee_year")
There is a gray at the edge of the sky, and the first drays on the stones, and the strange, constant, enormous sound of London waking up and finding itself a city. The house, wherever it is, is asleep. The lamp in the window is lit.
You have been in London for one night. There is a firm, and a roof, and a card, and a woman in a doorway, and a lock of hair in a frame. There is a man who has not come home. You think that there is going to be a good deal more.
